    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing righties. **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with a 76.91 score, bolstered by a prime #3 spot in the order and a favorable 4.46 xERA matchup against Mitch Keller. While **James Wood** (73.10) sits just behind him, he remains our most critical asset for the scarcity of stolen bases; his elite .407 xwOBA and high-leverage leadoff spot against Wacha make him a daily lock, despite the slight efficiency hit from the pitcher's hold profile. **Seiya Suzuki** (67.59) and **Brice Turang** (65.15) round out our tier-one starts, with **Brice Turang** offering high-upside speed potential against Cecconi, whose pace profiles favorably for potential swipes.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Alex Freeland** (38.92), who narrowly missed the starting cut as the optimizer prioritized maintaining game caps over his marginal ceiling against Drew Rasmussen. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting flexibility, the stiff 3.36 xERA of the opposing arm and his low-leverage spot in the order kept him below our 40-point threshold. We are monitoring **Corbin Carroll** (52.85) closely; despite his pedigree, the matchup against Detmers creates a significant SP Skill headwind (-19%), limiting his output. We are also proceeding without **Josh Naylor** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** due to lineup exclusions and injury status, respectively. With **Travis Bazzana**, **Cole Young**, **Jose Caballero**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Austin Riley** all checking in as moderate plays, we remain positioned to exploit the weak back-end of today\u2019s opposing rotations.",
